<DemoExample Title="Basic" RazorCode="@example1RazorCode" Id="example1">
    <div>
        Each option of the timeline renders a dot on the line, its PrimaryText before the line and its
        SecondaryText after it, so a single option can describe an event from both sides of the axis.
    </div>
    <br />
    <BitTimeline TItem="BitTimelineOption">
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 1" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 2" SecondaryText="Option 2 Secondary" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 3" />
    </BitTimeline>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Horizontal" RazorCode="@example2RazorCode" Id="example2" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>
        The Timeline offers two orientations: vertical (default) and horizontal. In the horizontal one the
        line runs from the start to the end of the timeline and the contents of each option stack above and
        below their dot.
    </div>
    <br />
    <BitTimeline TItem="BitTimelineOption" Horizontal>
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 1" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 2" SecondaryText="Option 2 Secondary" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 3" />
    </BitTimeline>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Disabled" RazorCode="@example3RazorCode" Id="example3" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>
        Disabling the whole timeline with IsEnabled dims every option and stops all of them from responding,
        while the IsEnabled of a single option only takes that one out of the interaction.
    </div>
    <br /><br /><br />
    <div>Disabled component</div><br />
    <BitTimeline TItem="BitTimelineOption" Horizontal IsEnabled="false">
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 1" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 2" SecondaryText="Option 2 Secondary" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 3" />
    </BitTimeline>
    <br /><br /><br />
    <div>Disabled item</div><br />
    <BitTimeline TItem="BitTimelineOption" Horizontal>
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 1" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 2" SecondaryText="Option 2 Secondary" IsEnabled="false" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 3" />
    </BitTimeline>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Variant" RazorCode="@example4RazorCode" Id="example4" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>
        The variant determines how the dots are painted: Fill (default) is a solid dot, Outline is a hollow
        dot with a colored border, and Text drops the dot's shape and keeps only its icon.
    </div>
    <br /><br /><br />
    <div>Fill</div><br />
    <BitTimeline Horizontal Variant="BitVariant.Fill" TItem="BitTimelineOption">
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 1" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 2" SecondaryText="Option 2 Secondary" IsEnabled="false" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 3" />
    </BitTimeline>
    <br /><br /><br />
    <div>Outline</div><br />
    <BitTimeline Horizontal Variant="BitVariant.Outline" TItem="BitTimelineOption">
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 1" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 2" SecondaryText="Option 2 Secondary" IsEnabled="false" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 3" />
    </BitTimeline>
    <br /><br /><br />
    <div>Text</div><br />
    <BitTimeline Horizontal Variant="BitVariant.Text" TItem="BitTimelineOption">
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 1" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 2" SecondaryText="Option 2 Secondary" IsEnabled="false" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 3" />
    </BitTimeline>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Icon" RazorCode="@example5RazorCode" Id="example5" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>
        Each option can render an icon inside its dot through IconName, which turns the dot into a marker of
        what the event actually was.
    </div>
    <br /><br /><br />
    <div>Fill</div><br />
    <BitTimeline Horizontal Variant="BitVariant.Fill" TItem="BitTimelineOption">
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 1" IconName="@BitIconName.Add" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 2" IconName="@BitIconName.Edit" SecondaryText="Option 2 Secondary" IsEnabled="false" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 3" IconName="@BitIconName.Delete" />
    </BitTimeline>
    <br /><br /><br />
    <div>Outline</div><br />
    <BitTimeline Horizontal Variant="BitVariant.Outline" TItem="BitTimelineOption">
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 1" IconName="@BitIconName.Add" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 2" IconName="@BitIconName.Edit" SecondaryText="Option 2 Secondary" IsEnabled="false" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 3" IconName="@BitIconName.Delete" />
    </BitTimeline>
    <br /><br /><br />
    <div>Text</div><br />
    <BitTimeline Horizontal Variant="BitVariant.Text" TItem="BitTimelineOption">
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 1" IconName="@BitIconName.Add" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 2" IconName="@BitIconName.Edit" SecondaryText="Option 2 Secondary" IsEnabled="false" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 3" IconName="@BitIconName.Delete" />
    </BitTimeline>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Reversed" RazorCode="@example6RazorCode" Id="example6" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>
        Reversed swaps the two sides of the line: on the timeline it flips every option at once, and on a
        single option it moves only that one to the opposite side.
    </div>
    <br /><br /><br />
    <div>Vertical</div><br />
    <div class="example-content">
        <BitTimeline TItem="BitTimelineOption" Reversed>
            <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 1" />
            <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 2" SecondaryText="Option 2 Secondary" />
            <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 3" />
        </BitTimeline>
        <BitTimeline TItem="BitTimelineOption">
            <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 1" />
            <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 2" Reversed />
            <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 3" />
        </BitTimeline>
    </div>
    <br /><br /><br />
    <div>Horizontal</div><br />
    <BitTimeline TItem="BitTimelineOption" Horizontal Reversed>
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 1" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 2" SecondaryText="Option 2 Secondary" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 3" />
    </BitTimeline>
    <br /><br />
    <BitTimeline TItem="BitTimelineOption" Horizontal>
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 1" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 2" Reversed />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 3" />
    </BitTimeline>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Alternate" RazorCode="@example7RazorCode" Id="example7" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>
        Alternate puts every second option on the opposite side of the line, so the options zig-zag around
        it. Combined with Reversed the zig-zag starts from the other side.
    </div>
    <br /><br /><br />
    <div>Vertical</div><br />
    <BitTimeline TItem="BitTimelineOption" Alternate>
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="09:00" SecondaryText="Option 1" IconName="@BitIconName.Add" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="10:30" SecondaryText="Option 2" IconName="@BitIconName.Edit" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="13:15" SecondaryText="Option 3" IconName="@BitIconName.Delete" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="16:45" SecondaryText="Option 4" IconName="@BitIconName.Accept" />
    </BitTimeline>
    <br /><br /><br />
    <div>Vertical & Reversed</div><br />
    <BitTimeline TItem="BitTimelineOption" Alternate Reversed>
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="09:00" SecondaryText="Option 1" IconName="@BitIconName.Add" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="10:30" SecondaryText="Option 2" IconName="@BitIconName.Edit" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="13:15" SecondaryText="Option 3" IconName="@BitIconName.Delete" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="16:45" SecondaryText="Option 4" IconName="@BitIconName.Accept" />
    </BitTimeline>
    <br /><br /><br />
    <div>Horizontal</div><br />
    <BitTimeline TItem="BitTimelineOption" Alternate Horizontal>
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="09:00" SecondaryText="Option 1" IconName="@BitIconName.Add" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="10:30" SecondaryText="Option 2" IconName="@BitIconName.Edit" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="13:15" SecondaryText="Option 3" IconName="@BitIconName.Delete" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="16:45" SecondaryText="Option 4" IconName="@BitIconName.Accept" />
    </BitTimeline>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Reverse order" RazorCode="@example8RazorCode" Id="example8" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>
        ReverseOrder renders the options from the last one to the first one, which turns a chronological
        list into a most-recent-first one without touching the markup itself.
    </div>
    <br /><br /><br />
    <div>Vertical</div><br />
    <BitTimeline TItem="BitTimelineOption" ReverseOrder>
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="09:00" SecondaryText="Option 1" IconName="@BitIconName.Add" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="10:30" SecondaryText="Option 2" IconName="@BitIconName.Edit" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="13:15" SecondaryText="Option 3" IconName="@BitIconName.Delete" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="16:45" SecondaryText="Option 4" IconName="@BitIconName.Accept" />
    </BitTimeline>
    <br /><br /><br />
    <div>Horizontal</div><br />
    <BitTimeline TItem="BitTimelineOption" ReverseOrder Horizontal>
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="09:00" SecondaryText="Option 1" IconName="@BitIconName.Add" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="10:30" SecondaryText="Option 2" IconName="@BitIconName.Edit" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="13:15" SecondaryText="Option 3" IconName="@BitIconName.Delete" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="16:45" SecondaryText="Option 4" IconName="@BitIconName.Accept" />
    </BitTimeline>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Truncate line" RazorCode="@example9RazorCode" Id="example9" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>
        By default the connecting line runs through the whole extent of the timeline, past the first and the
        last dot. TruncateLine cuts it back to the first dot (Start), to the last one (End), or to both (Both),
        which is what a self-contained timeline usually wants.
    </div>
    <br /><br /><br />
    <div>Both</div><br />
    <BitTimeline TItem="BitTimelineOption" TruncateLine="BitTimelineTruncateLine.Both">
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 1" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 2" SecondaryText="Option 2 Secondary" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 3" />
    </BitTimeline>
    <br /><br /><br />
    <div>Start</div><br />
    <BitTimeline TItem="BitTimelineOption" TruncateLine="BitTimelineTruncateLine.Start">
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 1" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 2" SecondaryText="Option 2 Secondary" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 3" />
    </BitTimeline>
    <br /><br /><br />
    <div>End</div><br />
    <BitTimeline TItem="BitTimelineOption" TruncateLine="BitTimelineTruncateLine.End">
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 1" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 2" SecondaryText="Option 2 Secondary" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 3" />
    </BitTimeline>
    <br /><br /><br />
    <div>Horizontal (Both)</div><br />
    <BitTimeline TItem="BitTimelineOption" Horizontal TruncateLine="BitTimelineTruncateLine.Both">
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 1" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 2" SecondaryText="Option 2 Secondary" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Option 3" />
    </BitTimeline>
</DemoExample>

<DemoExample Title="Item customization" RazorCode="@example10RazorCode" Id="example10" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>
        Color, Size and Variant are also available on the option itself, where they override the values of
        the timeline for that option alone, and HideDot drops the dot of an option while keeping its
        contents in place.
    </div>
    <br />
    <BitTimeline TItem="BitTimelineOption">
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Success" IconName="@BitIconName.Accept" Color="BitColor.Success" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Warning" IconName="@BitIconName.Warning" Color="BitColor.Warning" Variant="BitVariant.Outline" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="Error" IconName="@BitIconName.ErrorBadge" Color="BitColor.Error" Size="BitSize.Large" />
        <BitTimelineOption PrimaryText="No dot" HideDot />
    </BitTimeline>
</DemoExample>

